title: 'Update EVM Opcode Benchmarking and Weights'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Replace JUMPDEST-based estimates for selected EVM opcodes with
    weights derived from their own benchmarks. Add charges for memory
    expansion and for copying RETURN/REVERT output from EVM memory.

    The `evm_opcode` benchmark and WeightInfo method are renamed to
    `evm_jumpdest_opcode`. Rename the method in custom WeightInfo
    implementations and update its callers.

    The following benchmarks and matching WeightInfo methods are added:

    - `evm_jump_opcode`
    - `evm_jumpi_opcode`
    - `evm_jumpi_opcode_always_taken`
    - `evm_jumpi_opcode_always_not_taken`
    - `evm_pc_opcode`
    - `evm_push_opcode`
    - `evm_dup_opcode`
    - `evm_swap_opcode`
    - `evm_chainid_opcode`
    - `evm_difficulty_opcode`
    - `evm_codesize_opcode`
    - `evm_calldatasize_opcode`
    - `evm_returndatasize_opcode`
    - `evm_calldataload_opcode`
    - `evm_memory_grow`
    - `evm_memory_reallocate`
    - `evm_memory_copy_out`
    - `evm_mload_opcode`
    - `evm_msize_opcode`
    - `evm_mstore_opcode`
    - `evm_mstore8_opcode`
    - `evm_mcopy_opcode`
    - `evm_mcopy_per_byte`
    - `evm_lt_opcode`
    - `evm_gt_opcode`
    - `evm_eq_opcode`
    - `evm_iszero_opcode`
    - `evm_and_opcode`
    - `evm_or_opcode`
    - `evm_xor_opcode`
    - `evm_not_opcode`
    - `evm_byte_opcode`
    - `evm_clz_opcode`
    - `evm_slt_opcode`
    - `evm_sgt_opcode`
    - `evm_shl_opcode`
    - `evm_shr_opcode`
    - `evm_sar_opcode`
    - `evm_add_opcode`
    - `evm_sub_opcode`
    - `evm_mul_opcode`
    - `evm_exp_zero_opcode`
    - `evm_exp_opcode`
    - `evm_exp_per_bit`
    - `evm_signextend_opcode`
    - `evm_dispatch_mix`

    Regenerate pallet-revive weights for your runtime and implement these
    methods in custom WeightInfo implementations. Update exhaustive
    matches on RuntimeCosts for the new memory cost variants.

    No storage migration is required.
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    EVM execution charges change. Some opcode charges decrease, while
    memory expansion and RETURN/REVERT output copying now incur
    additional charges.

    Existing contracts do not need migration or redeployment. Re-estimate
    gas limits after the runtime upgrade; calls using previous limits
    may run out of gas.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
